(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/plugin.asl#" :text "Provider plugin contract: a capability record and a plugin record of fn values; the core reaches a provider only through its record, and lifecycle operations that spend pass budget.asl's spend gate.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/plugin.asl#Batching" :text "design section 2 names the third case none; unbatched avoids shadowing the Option constructor")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/plugin.asl#Plugin" :text "sendBatch exists only for batchEndpoint providers; lifecycle only for providers that deploy or scale")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/plugin.asl#makePlugin" :text "the only constructor, so every plugin record the core sees satisfies the contract")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/plugin.asl#gatedLifecycle!" :text "a spending operation runs only when budget/gate allows its action; no ledger means no spend")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/plugin.asl#ungatedLifecycle!" :text "stop and status never spend, so they need no ledger: stopping must work when the budget is exhausted")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/plugin.asl#followingRedirects" :text "a provider that answers long requests with a 303 every redirectAfterSec seconds (Modal: 150) is followed for as many hops as its timeout allows")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/plugin.asl#openaiCompat" :text "one adapter for every OpenAI-compatible HTTP provider; a provider is a URL and key row, never a code branch")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/plugin.asl#defaultPlugins!" :text "every HTTP row is an openaiCompat plugin, CLI rows get their own dispatch; a failed constructor fails the registry")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/plugin.asl#pluginWithLifecycle" :text "a lifecycle comes from config after the row's plugin exists; the scale model travels with it so the core reads serverless timings from capabilities")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/plugin.asl#sendHttp!" :text "the core's HTTP send: look the provider's plugin up by id and start the call through its record")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/poolDispatch.asl#" :text "Runs one batchPool state machine per (provider, model): arrivals, ticks and finished upstream calls go in; upstream calls, client replies and the scale-down hook come out.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/poolDispatch.asl#poolWithPlugins" :text "pool lanes send through the provider plugins the server loaded from the gateway config")
